cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below, and cite the original sources listed in the README."
title: "Oil market dataset: monthly real oil price, world oil production, global crude inventories, WECI and geopolitical risk, 1974m1–2026m10"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Morão"
    given-names: "Hugo"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hmorao95/oil_market_dataset"
url: "https://github.com/hmorao95/oil_market_dataset"
abstract: >-
  Five monthly series for oil market VARs, from January 1974: the real
  refiners' acquisition cost of imported crude oil, world crude oil
  production growth, the change in global crude oil inventories (Kilian and
  Murphy 2014), the world economic conditions indicator of Baumeister,
  Korobilis and Lee (2022), and the historical geopolitical risk index of
  Caldara and Iacoviello (2022). Built from public EIA, BLS, Baumeister and
  Caldara-Iacoviello data, with the Python code used to download and build it.
keywords:
  - oil market
  - crude oil
  - inventories
  - structural VAR
  - EIA
  - time series
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Petroleum and international energy data (API v2)"
    authors:
      - name: "U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)"
    url: "https://www.eia.gov/opendata/"
  - type: article
    title: "The role of inventories and speculative trading in the global market for crude oil"
    authors:
